Backport of apache/datafusion#24456 (cost-based join order enumeration, DPhyp) onto
DataFusion 55.0.0, for the dfrunner `jo` build (engines `df-jo`, `df-jo-cs`).

Source: Dandandan/datafusion branch perf/join-order-enumeration, PR head
472e83e1289eec0b482a5b3d4d0dc1f5140fe878, diffed against its merge base with main,
242b96c231636b5738125678a83197896a5cc64b (the PR's own changes only). Taken: every
non-test source file of the PR (datafusion-common, datafusion-physical-optimizer,
datafusion-physical-plan). Left out: tests, sqllogictest files and docs.
The head already contains its own copy of the join total_byte_size change from
apache/datafusion#24536 (joins/utils.rs); that copy is what is applied here.
apache/datafusion#24517, #24520 and #24558 (merged after 55.0.0) are not included: the
code compiles without them (checked), and #24558 would change hash_join_single_partition_threshold
for every join, not only reordered ones.

Applied to the crates.io 55.0.0 sources of those three crates (identical to the 55.0.0
tag's src/); paths below are the apache/datafusion repository's.
Conflicts resolved against 55.0.0 (main had moved on):
- common/src/config.rs: keep 55.0.0's `use_statistics_registry` option (main
  deprecated it); add `join_enumeration` (default true) and `join_enumeration_limit`.
- physical-optimizer/src/join_selection.rs: keep 55.0.0's statistics lookup (registry
  only with `use_statistics_registry`); add the PR's `keep_partitioning_needed_above`
  pass, taking that registry instead of the optimizer context.
- physical-optimizer/src/join_enumeration/mod.rs: statistics come from where 55.0.0's
  JoinSelection takes them (main's `StatisticsContext::new_with_registry` does not
  exist in 55.0.0).
Compile fixes for 55.0.0 (no behaviour change):
- physical-plan/src/filter.rs: import `InListExpr` (main imported it already).
- join_enumeration/mod.rs: `default_filter_selectivity` is a plain u8 in 55.0.0 (no `.get()`).
Not taken: the PR's tests. Behaviour that differs from plain 55.0.0 even with
`join_enumeration=false`: JoinSelection's new `keep_partitioning_needed_above` pass and
the filter estimates (per conjunct, IN lists) in physical-plan/src/filter.rs.

